## What can be uploaded

**Any car-related part file** — 3D print models, scans, cutting profiles, and 2D drawings. STEP is preferred where you have it. Multiple STEP, STL, and additional files per submission are fine and encouraged.

**Function over decoration.** Zenthi is not for trinkets or purely aesthetic items. The goal is to cut through the noise of the broader 3D-printing community — which is dominated by novelty items — and build something genuinely useful.

Not accepted:

- Rose-shaped cup holder inserts
- Keychains
- Phone holders
- Decorative shift knobs
- Novelty coasters
- Anything whose primary purpose is looks rather than solving a real fitment, repair, or fabrication problem

**Safety-critical items** — brakes, suspension, structural, fuel-carrying — are welcome as reference and fitment data only.

> ⚠️ Printed polymer has no business holding a car together or containing fuel.

**Restricted brands.** Parts for the following cannot be listed, for legal-risk reasons:

- Honda, Acura
- Stellantis brands: Chrysler, Dodge, Jeep, Ram, Fiat, Alfa Romeo, Maserati, Peugeot, Citroën, DS, Opel, Vauxhall, Lancia, Abarth

**Licensing.** Reuploads need a source link, the original creator's name, and the correct license. Modified files need the original's license. ND-licensed originals (CC BY-ND, CC BY-NC-ND) cannot be reshared as modifications.

---

## What admins check before approving

- [ ] The category matches what the part actually is
- [ ] Fitment data is present and plausible — make, model, year range, engine details
- [ ] Licensing is valid: source link, creator credit, and the ND / modification rules
- [ ] No restricted-brand fitment
- [ ] No obvious copyright problems — scraped commercial files, paid models, or ripped OEM CAD
- [ ] Safety-critical parts are flagged reference-only

---

## Admin conduct expectations

- **Don't approve your own submissions** — leave them for another admin.
- **Act in good faith.** Approve on the merits, not on who uploaded it.
- Repeated bad-faith approvals, or approving around these rules, can result in the admin role being removed at the discretion of other admins or the site owner.

---

## How to become an admin

Create an account, then submit a short request explaining why you'd be a good reviewer — your background with car parts, CAD, scanning, or moderating communities. An existing admin reviews the request and either grants the admin role or declines it. You'll see the status on your account page.

You don't need an account to browse the library or use the search engine. Accounts are only needed for uploading, posting or fulfilling requests, and admin actions.

**[Sign in and request admin access →](https://zenthi3d.lovable.app/account)**
